  "acceptance": [
    "The native box-publication owner validates shared structural dimensions independently of owner/analysis presence, before publication or invalidation. Twelve formerly failing standalone/analysis-free public/native/property controls now reject atomically; the six existing named-analysis controls are retained.",
    "Retain the declared exact-cardinality contract: one cell per addressed structure, without implicit broadcasting. Valid whole/nonconsecutive updates preserve source time/coordinate/label axes under nm and pm policies and ordinary/trusted delegation. None clearing, empty-selection no-op and historical snapshot/analysis scope are tested.",
    "Fresh Structures payload construction has an explicit transient initialization scope and retains complete final alignment validation. The scope is removed even after failure; existing edits have no persistent construction bypass.",
    "47 direct semantic controls are included in 2,481 affected native/form/set/analysis/persistence cases. All pass without skips. The clean source also passes 116 registered scientific cases across 74 nodes.",
    "No Rust, detector, provider floor, schema or scientific criterion is changed. The existing ArgDigest, PyUnitWizard conversion and SMonitor structural exception boundaries remain the owners."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This is one-attribute prepublication integrity, not a rollback promise for an arbitrary multi-key msm.set transaction or unsynchronized raw external writes.",
    "A single cell is not auto-expanded; callers wanting uniform cells explicitly supply one per addressed structure. New box-only construction can define its sole axis, unlike conflicting coordinate/time series.",
    "Source controls do not qualify a package, other platforms, a GUI family or a release. The supplemental correction receives no additional milestone weight. Full combined HTML/fast/client receiving follows separately."
  ]
